# Development Workflow

## Prerequisites

- Bun 1.3+ (required for build **and** runtime)

## Common Commands

```bash
bun install            # deps + Husky pre-commit (Biome on staged files)
bun run src/index.ts   # dev run from source
bun run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit
bun run lint           # biome check src/
bun run format         # biome format src/   (fix: bun run format:fix)
bun run test           # vitest
bun run build          # scripts/build.ts → dist/index.js + dist/shelra.exe (+ per-user install)
SHELRA_BUILD_SKIP_INSTALL=1 bun run build   # build artifacts only
bun run dist/index.js  # run the built CLI (Bun only; node fails on bun:sqlite)
```

## Environment Variables

The default path is cloud-first OpenRouter Free and needs an OpenRouter key.
The managed local path is explicit through `--local`; copy `.env.example` to
`.env` for the full list.

| Variable | Purpose |
|----|----|
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | Primary cloud provider key; activates dynamic Free catalog and routing. |
| `SHELRA_API_KEY` / `SHELRA_BASE_URL` | Optional generic OpenAI-compatible provider (`--remote`). Legacy `GROK_*` still read. |
| `SHELRA_MODEL` | Force a model id for every turn |
| `SHELRA_RUNTIME_BACKEND` | `cpu` or `cuda` for the managed llama.cpp engine (auto-detected) |
| `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` | Enable the Telegram bridge |

Every agent task also performs bounded web research, prioritizing Google when
available and falling back only when Google cannot return usable results.

## Git hooks

`bun install` sets up **Husky** → **lint-staged**, which runs
`biome check --write` on staged `*.{ts,tsx,js,mjs,cjs,json}` and re-stages fixes.

## Before submitting changes

1. `bun run format` and `bun run lint` — CI blocks on both (Biome).
2. `bun run typecheck` — CI enforces.
3. `bun run test`.
4. `bun run build` — CI runs `build:binary`.
5. No secrets or `.env` files committed.

## Project structure conventions

- Source in `src/`, compiled output in `dist/` (gitignored unless built locally).
- CLI entry is `src/index.ts` (Commander) → OpenTUI React shell in `src/ui/`.
- `ShelraCode/` is a gitignored migration reference checkout — do not edit it.
- Line endings are CRLF repo-wide (`biome.json` + `.gitattributes`).
